  "verbalization": "Peperomin B is implicated in the relationship with NCI-H446 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Peperomin B to SF-188, which is a target of a complex molecule, and SF-188 is ultimately targeted by NCI-H446. The second pathway connects Peperomin B to Carboxylesterase 2, which is targeted by a compound, and Carboxylesterase 2 is also targeted by NCI-H446. The third pathway connects Peperomin B to MOVP-3, which targets Npc15336, which in turn targets NCI-H446. These pathways suggest that Peperomin B may influence NCI-H446 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving enzyme activity or receptor binding. The evidence supports a mechanism where Peperomin B exerts a functional effect on NCI-H446 via a chain of targets, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Peperomin B in modulating NCI-H446 through a complex network of molecular targets.",
